<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Gisaka</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1852 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An eastern rival of the Kingdom of Rwanda, ruled by its own dynasty until Rwanda annexed it in the mid-19th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Gisaka occupied the lands of south-eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Rwanda</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kagera-river">Kagera river</a>. Its rulers belonged to the Bagesera clan, and court traditions present it as one of the older kingdoms of the region, already established when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyiginya-dynasty">Nyiginya dynasty</a> of the Kingdom of Rwanda was still small.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Gisaka was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>-keeping and farming kingdom with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacred-kingship">sacred kingship</a>, royal drums and rituals similar to those of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Rwanda</a>. For generations it fought Rwanda over borderlands and cattle, at times defeating its rival in the 17th and 18th centuries, according to Rwandan court traditions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Rwanda</a> conquered and annexed Gisaka around 1852 under Mwami <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutara-ii-rwogera">Mutara II Rwogera</a>. In the colonial period the British briefly claimed the region in 1919 before it returned to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ruanda-urundi">Belgian Ruanda-Urundi</a>. Gisaka's identity survived as a region of eastern Rwanda.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1852 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:7.00%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1852 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kinyarwanda</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/rwanda">Rwanda</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gisaka</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1676&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gisaka" aria-label="Kingdom of Gisaka on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5512 2252 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Gisaka lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5826 2522h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5832 2508h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5832 2508h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Rwanda. <a href="/atlas?year=1676&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gisaka">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

